# Shared Contracts Contributor Guide

This file supplements the repository-level `AGENTS.md` for `@imsweb/contracts`.
The package is a private workspace dependency of `@imsweb/api` and `@imsweb/web`;
it is the only shared source for cross-workspace wire contracts.

## Ownership and boundaries

- Keep API↔Web response schemas, their `z.infer`/`z.input` wire types, shared
  success envelopes, page-info combinators, and URL path definitions here.
- Keep Web-only request/input schemas, `File`/`FormData` shapes, UI-semantic
  aliases, and endpoint functions in `apps/web`.
- Keep API ports, persistence Records, database models, error bodies, redirects,
  and media stream boundaries in `apps/api`.
- The package must never depend on either application workspace, API runtime
  modules, Web UI modules, database drivers, or object-storage adapters.

## Layout and exports

Use flat-first organization: one file per business domain. Promote a domain to a
folder only after it needs multiple related files, and mirror that folder with an
`exports` subpath in `package.json`. The root `src/index.ts` exposes only
camelCase namespaces; business code imports the narrow subpath instead of the
root namespace. Shared atoms are exported only by their owning core module.
Admin schemas use an `admin` prefix, and multi-source modules place public
schemas before admin schemas.

`src/common.ts` owns composable success envelopes and page-info schemas.
`src/paths.ts` owns shared API, middleware, cookie-scope, and public-delivery
prefixes. Prefixes are declared once; callers keep only business suffixes and
dynamic parameters. A path change must be made here and consumed by both
applications.

## zod and build contract

This is the only package allowed to declare or directly import `zod`. The
package's `src/z.ts` is the supported zod entry point for consumers. Keep schema
output as the wire contract; export `z.input` variants only where coercion or
transformation means the API's emitted shape requires them. The package builds
CommonJS with declarations under `dist/`, and `prepare` must remain safe when
source files are not present during a Docker manifest-only install.

Every new wire-contract module must be added to the package `exports` map, the
root camelCase namespace index, and `packages/contracts/README.md`; repository-level documentation standards are in
`docs/README.md`. Avoid
barrel re-exports that make sibling atom names ambiguous.

## Validation

Run from the repository root:

```sh
pnpm --filter @imsweb/contracts run build
pnpm run check:rules
pnpm run check:boundaries
pnpm --filter @imsweb/web run typecheck
pnpm --filter @imsweb/api run typecheck
```

When a schema changes, update the consuming endpoint and API response aliases
and add or extend an HTTP response conformance assertion. Do not edit generated
contract copies: there is no generated Web/API duplicate ledger.
